 "text": " Every agent demo ends the same way. The agent buys the thing, everyone claps, and nobody asks what happens when it buys the wrong thing. Leash is the part that says no. You write a mandate, a total, a ceiling per purchase, which merchants, which categories, how fast. The agent gets a goal, not a budget, never touches a payment credential. Every purchase it tries runs 11 checks before any money moves. And when it is refused, it is not just blocked, it is told what would appear. This is the idea. This is it running for real. One man did $500, a hundred a purchase, named merchants, named categories. Now send an agent at it with a goal and no budget. Find me an office chair. A model chooses a product that is the only decision it gets to make. Refused on the ceiling told what would clear and it came back inside Now the part that I actually cared about Tell an agent nothing over a hundred and a competent one does not give up It splits the purchase. 75 to ACME US, 75 to ACME EU, each clears the cap. Only the cluster does not. Refused as structuring. approved spend settles through PayPal payouts real patches real money a sandbox account on the other side same amounts in PayPal's own books and comes off one click mid session every unsettled hold is dropped money that already moved stays moved the agent does not know anything changed it It keeps asking, it keeps getting nothing. Two red teams, one of them was a model. Three hundred and twenty two attempts, zero breaches. Every other demo shows you what their agent can't buy, this one shows you what he cannot. Thank you.",
